P0090... P0573.\\n    -   I will write P01 focusing on tumor heterogeneity using the specific cohort/review sources assigned.\\n    -   I will write P02 focusing on model differences (mouse vs human) using the review sources (P0535, P0146, P0573) to discuss the evidence gap.\\n    -   I will create the Table using the remaining sources (P0080, P0388, P0269, P0438) for the rows where they are assigned, and reuse the others where assigned in `table_tasks`.\\n\\n2.  **Draft Paragraph 2:** Focus on the evidence hierarchy. Mouse models (causal) vs Human (observational). Use P0535, P0146, P0573 to discuss the limitations of extrapolation.\\n\\n3.  **Draft Table:** Follow the `table_tasks` structure. Ensure columns match. Fill cells with specific findings from the assigned sources.\\n\\n**Refining P01:**\\n-   Start with the thesis: Mechanisms are not universal; they depend on tumor type.\\n-   Melanoma: High immunogenicity, T-cell cross-reactivity dominates (P0146, P0573).\\n-   NSCLC: Lung microbiome independent of gut, metabolic microenvironment (adenosine) (P0352).\\n-   GI Tumors (HCC/CRC): Barrier integrity, etiology (viral vs metabolic) matters (P0113, P0457).\\n-   Counter-examples/Heterogeneity: RCC (antibiotics impact) (P0090), Prostate (A. muciniphila negative correlation) (P0270), TNBC (chemo vs ICI difference) (P0057).\\n-   Synthesis: Intratumoral vs Gut (P0535).\\n\\n**Refining P02:**\\n-   Transition: This heterogeneity is compounded by the evidence source (model vs human).\\n-   Mouse: Causal (FMT, KO) (P0146, P0573).\\n-   Human: Observational (cohorts, markers) (P0535).\\n-   Risk: Over-extrapolation.\\n\\n**Refining Table:**\\n-   Columns: 肿瘤类型，关键微生物特征，主要机制/通路，证据类型，来源.\\n-   Rows: As per `table_tasks`.\\n-   Ensure specific numbers/findings from sources are accurate (e.g., P0270 A. muciniphila negative, P0090 Antibiotics HR).\\n\\n**Check Constraints:**\\n-   JSON output.\\n-   No author/year in text.\\n-   Citations `[Pxxxx]`.\\n-   Chinese language.\\n-   Issues list if any (e.g., if material is missing for a table cell).\\n\\n**Material Check:**\\n-   P0080: Melanoma, LPS hexa-acylated, TLR4.\\n-   P0388: Melanoma, SFB, T cell plasticity.\\n-   P0269: Review, host factors, adenosine/metabolites mentioned? P0269 `study_summary_A` mentions \\\"metabolic modulation (short-chain fatty acids, inosine)\\\". `table_tasks` asks for \\\"Adenosine metabolic microenvironment\\\" for NSCLC. P0269 is a general review. P0352 is specific to NSCLC lung microbiome. P0269 might not have specific NSCLC adenosine data. I need to check `table_tasks` row 2: \\\"NSCLC... Adenosine...\\\". Source uses: P0352, P0269. P0352 `study_summary_A` mentions \\\"metabolic profiles favoring lipid metabolism and essential amino acid degradation\\\". It doesn't explicitly say \\\"adenosine\\\". P0269 `study_summary_A` mentions \\\"inosine\\\". I need to be careful not to hallucinate \\\"adenosine\\\" if the material says \\\"inosine\\\" or \\\"lipid/amino acid\\\". The `table_tasks` *prompt* says \\\"Adenosine\\\". I must check if the *source* supports \\\"Adenosine\\\". P0269 mentions \\\"inosine\\\". P0352 mentions \\\"lipid/amino acid\\\". I should write what the source says, not what the task prompt implies if it contradicts. I will write \\\"Metabolic modulation (lipid/amino acid/inosine)\\\" to be accurate to the source.\\n-   P0438: GI cancer, barrier, F. nucleatum.\\n-   P0057: TNBC, TMAO, pyroptosis.\\n-   P0270: Prostate, A. muciniphila negative.\\n-   P0113: HCC, etiology (HBV vs NASH).\\n-   P0090: RCC, Antibiotics HR 1.96-3.10.\\n-   P0146: Review, general mechanisms.\\n-   P0535: Intratumoral vs Gut.\\n\\n**Issues:**\\n-   Table Row 2 (NSCLC) asks for \\\"Adenosine\\\". P0352 mentions \\\"lipid/amino acid\\\". P0269 mentions \\\"inosine\\\". I will note this nuance in the table cell to remain faithful to the material.\\n-   Table Row 1 (Melanoma) asks for \\\"Hexa-acylated LPS\\\". P0080 supports this. \\\"T cell cross-reactivity\\\"