le cell).\n\n**Material Check:**\n-   P0080: Melanoma, LPS hexa-acylated, TLR4.\n-   P0388: Melanoma, SFB, T cell plasticity.\n-   P0269: Review, host factors, adenosine/metabolites mentioned? P0269 `study_summary_A` mentions \"metabolic modulation (short-chain fatty acids, inosine)\". `table_tasks` asks for \"Adenosine metabolic microenvironment\" for NSCLC. P0269 is a general review. P0352 is specific to NSCLC lung microbiome. P0269 might not have specific NSCLC adenosine data. I need to check `table_tasks` row 2: \"NSCLC... Adenosine...\". Source uses: P0352, P0269. P0352 `study_summary_A` mentions \"metabolic profiles favoring lipid metabolism and essential amino acid degradation\". It doesn't explicitly say \"adenosine\". P0269 `study_summary_A` mentions \"inosine\". I need to be careful not to hallucinate \"adenosine\" if the material says \"inosine\" or \"lipid/amino acid\". The `table_tasks` *prompt* says \"Adenosine\". I must check if the *source* supports \"Adenosine\". P0269 mentions \"inosine\". P0352 mentions \"lipid/amino acid\". I should write what the source says, not what the task prompt implies if it contradicts. I will write \"Metabolic modulation (lipid/amino acid/inosine)\" to be accurate to the source.\n-   P0438: GI cancer, barrier, F. nucleatum.\n-   P0057: TNBC, TMAO, pyroptosis.\n-   P0270: Prostate, A. muciniphila negative.\n-   P0113: HCC, etiology (HBV vs NASH).\n-   P0090: RCC, Antibiotics HR 1.96-3.10.\n-   P0146: Review, general mechanisms.\n-   P0535: Intratumoral vs Gut.\n\n**Issues:**\n-   Table Row 2 (NSCLC) asks for \"Adenosine\". P0352 mentions \"lipid/amino acid\". P0269 mentions \"inosine\". I will note this nuance in the table cell to remain faithful to the material.\n-   Table Row 1 (Melanoma) asks for \"Hexa-acylated LPS\". P0080 supports this. \"T cell cross-reactivity\". P0388 supports this (SFB molecular mimicry).\n\nLet's assemble the text.\n\n**Paragraph 1:**\nStart with the variability. Melanoma has strong evidence for T-cell cross-reactivity and LPS structure [P0146][P0573]. NSCLC shows independent lung microbiome effects [P0352]. GI tumors depend on etiology [P0113]. RCC sensitive to antibiotics [P0090]. Prostate shows reverse correlation for Akkermansia [P0270]. TNBC shows chemo vs ICI difference [P0057]. Intratumoral bacteria also play a role [P0535][P0457].\n\n**Paragraph 2:**\nDistinguish evidence. Mouse models allow causal inference (FMT, KO) [P0146][P0573]. Human data is largely observational (cohorts, sequencing) [P0535]. Extrapolation risk [P0146].\n\n**Table:**\nFill rows based on `table_tasks` and source content.\n\n**JSON Structure:**\n`{\"body_markdown\": \"...\", \"issues\": []}`\n\n**Self-Correction on Citation Reuse:**\nThe instruction says \"同一篇可以跨段使用，但用途必须不同\" (Same paper can be used across paragraphs, but usage must be different).\nP0535, P0146, P0573 are in P01 and P02.\nIn P01: Used for tumor type examples.\nIn P02: Used for model system evidence levels.\nThis is acceptable.\nP0080, P0388, P0269, P0438 are *only* in Table tasks. I will cite them in the table cells.\nP0057, P0090, P0113, P0270, P0352, P0457 are in P01 and Table. I will cite them in P01 text, and can cite them again in the table if needed for specific data points, but to avoid clutter, I might rely on the text for the general claim and table for the specific comparison. However, the Table Task says \"Source\" column. I must put the citation in the table cell. So `[P0090]` will appear in P01 text and Table Row 3. This is allowed as long as the *content* isn't mechanically repeated (Text: narrative; Table: structured comparison).\n\nLet's write.",
